  "question": {
    "text": "Let a circle $C$ of radius 1 and closer to the origin be such that the lines passing through the point $(3,2)$ and parallel to the coordinate axes touch it. Then the shortest distance of the circle $\\mathrm{C}$ from the point $(5,5)$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "3xFeF",
      "text": "$2 \\sqrt{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jgLm6",
      "text": "$4 \\sqrt{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "hrMYd",
      "text": "4",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AomRl",
      "text": "5",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/TaIPB9MRQkEpWyAhHYRzdbglbv0mY_NI9h8hoTylNYw.original.fullsize.png\"><br />Coordinates of the centre will be $(2,1)$\nEquation of circle will be\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& (\\mathrm{x}-2)^2+(\\mathrm{y}-1)^2=1 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{QC}=\\sqrt{(5-2)^2+(5-1)^2} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{QC}=5\n\\end{aligned}$\nshortest distance\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& =\\mathrm{RQ}=\\mathrm{CQ}-\\mathrm{CR} \\\\\n& =5-1 \\\\\n& =4\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
